{"id":"20260825T180823.797303136Z-ee226dc1","time":"2026-08-25T18:08:23.797303136Z","session_id":"session-20260825T180823.796926375Z","task_id":"task-1787681303797232210","source":"system","kind":"task.created","summary":"Scrolling the transcript responds only to PgUp/PgDn, which terminals and multiplexers routinely capture for their own scrollback before the program sees it, and a single-line scroll is undone immediately so the keys appear dead.\n\nMake scrolling respond to what a reader actually reaches for: the arrow keys, the usual ctrl bindings, and the mouse wheel. One notch must move exactly one line and must not be clamped back. Scrolling down must move towards the newest output, and the transcript must keep reporting how many earlier lines are hidden. How the position is stored is yours to decide."}
