{"id":"20260825T181118.315166445Z-4388198e","time":"2026-08-25T18:11:18.315166445Z","session_id":"session-20260825T180823.796926375Z","task_id":"task-1787681303797232210","source":"architect","kind":"output","summary":"{\"decision\":\"proceed\",\"message\":\"\",\"summary\":\"Make transcript scrolling line-accurate and accessible through arrows, Ctrl-P/Ctrl-N, and the mouse wheel without changing provider or workflow authority behavior.\",\"plan\":\"Modify only the TUI transcript viewport and its focused tests. Use one shared wrapped-row viewport calculation for rendering and scrolling, persist the effective bounded position after every input, retain existing page and return-to-bottom controls, enable Bubble Tea wheel reporting, and keep the hidden-earlier-line count derived from the displayed top row.\",\"steps\":[\"Centralize transcript viewport bounds so input handling and rendering use the same wrapped-row and available-height calculation.\",\"Map Up and Ctrl-P to exactly one earlier line, and Down and Ctrl-N to exactly one newer line, while retaining PgUp, PgDn, Shift-Up, Shift-Down, and Ctrl-G behavior.\",\"Enable Bubble Tea cell-motion mouse reporting and map each wheel-up or wheel-down event to exactly one transcript line in the corresponding direction.\",\"Persist the effective scroll position after movement so render-time bounds cannot undo a one-line step; resume following output when movement reaches the newest row.\",\"Render the earlier-lines indicator from the effective viewport top and update its control hint to describe the accessible bindings.\",\"Add input-boundary regression tests covering arrows, Ctrl-P/Ctrl-N, wheel direction and one-line granularity, movement from both bounds, unclamped repeated movement, newest-output following, and accurate hidden-line counts.\",\"Run gofmt, go vet ./..., and go test ./..., plus the exact Sensei checks required by the task briefing and final admitted envelope.\"],\"consequences\":\"Readers can scroll the transcript one rendered line at a time with conventional keyboard and wheel inputs; down consistently approaches the newest output, reaching the bottom restores follow mode, and the indicator continues to report the number of earlier rendered lines hidden. Provider credentials, workflow authority, and command behavior remain unchanged.\",\"files\":[\"internal/tui/model.go\",\"internal/tui/scroll_test.go\"],\"mode\":\"modify\",\"related_invariants\":[\"invariant:sensei_code.provider.credentials_remain_provider_owned\"],\"human_question\":\"\",\"recommendation\":\"\",\"options\":[],\"claims\":[{\"statement\":\"Model.Update currently offers transcript scrolling only from KeyPressMsg, and Model.scroll recognizes PgUp, PgDn, Shift-Up, Shift-Down, and Ctrl-G.\",\"about\":\"internal/tui/model.go\",\"source\":\"repository\"},{\"statement\":\"Model.View computes wrapped transcript rows and clamps a local top position without persisting that effective position back into the model.\",\"about\":\"internal/tui/model.go\",\"source\":\"repository\"},{\"statement\":\"The current view does not enable a Bubble Tea mouse mode, and the update path has no MouseWheelMsg handling.\",\"about\":\"internal/tui/model.go\",\"source\":\"repository\"},{\"statement\":\"The repository uses Bubble Tea v2.0.8, whose MouseWheelMsg distinguishes MouseWheelUp and MouseWheelDown and whose MouseModeCellMotion enables wheel events.\",\"about\":\"charm.land/bubbletea/v2 and go.mod\",\"source\":\"repository\"},{\"statement\":\"The current checkout has no internal/tui/scroll_test.go, although the preceding scrollability change historically introduced that focused test file and the benchmark commit removed it.\",\"about\":\"internal/tui/scroll_test.go\",\"source\":\"repository\"},{\"statement\":\"Provider credential ownership is a critical active invariant directly anchored to internal/tui/model.go.\",\"about\":\"internal/tui/model.go\",\"source\":\"graph\"},{\"statement\":\"The targeted scrolling, viewport, and rendering paths do not read, write, or transfer provider credentials.\",\"about\":\"internal/tui/model.go\",\"source\":\"repository\"},{\"statement\":\"Using the same effective viewport bounds for scrolling and rendering will prevent a one-line movement from being visually reversed by render-only clamping.\",\"about\":\"transcript viewport state\",\"source\":\"inference\"}]}","payload":{"stream":"assistant"}}
