crollability change historically introduced that focused test file and the benchmark commit removed it. (internal/tui/scroll_test.go) — source: repository\n  [evidence-bearing] Provider credential ownership is a critical active invariant directly anchored to internal/tui/model.go. (internal/tui/model.go) — source: graph\n  [evidence-bearing] The targeted scrolling, viewport, and rendering paths do not read, write, or transfer provider credentials. (internal/tui/model.go) — source: repository\n  [NEEDS EVIDENCE] Using the same effective viewport bounds for scrolling and rendering will prevent a one-line movement from being visually reversed by render-only clamping. (transcript viewport state) — source: inference\n  the objective does not establish any of these. Evidence does.\n\nconsequence decision:\n  BOUNDED — the candidate worktree: files are edited in an isolated checkout, the diff is audited before it leaves, and discarding the worktree leaves the world unchanged\n  assessed from the action, not from who asked and not from whether the plan satisfies the objective.\n\nrouted: human-authority-required\n"}
